-- NEW and OLD — The Most Important Concept
NEW: Represents the new row values.

Used with:
INSERT
UPDATE

Example:
NEW.total_amount
NEW.status
NEW.order_id

OLD: Represents the previous row values.
Used with:
UPDATE
DELETE

Example:
OLD.total_amount
OLD.status
OLD.order_id

-> MySQL defines OLD as the existing value before an update/delete and NEW as the incoming/new value for insert/update

 Event   OLD       NEW 
 INSERT | No     |  Yes     
 UPDATE | Yes     | Yes     
 DELETE | Yes     | No     

